# I04.var03 v1.0.0 pre-native publication routing — NO_GO

The frozen 119-file owned source inventory and 322-record prelaunch manifest exclude the whole `runs/` subtree. The root-level package README and reproduction guide describe that tree as the reserved native run location, and `.gitignore` ignores it. The normal catalog and evidence-index flow publishes source, review and an evidence index as tracked package files while retaining native raw in ignored runs.

Placing new publication docs and an index under `runs/publication-i04-var03-v1.0.0/` and force-adding them would technically permit a hashable postrun bundle, but it would introduce a new catalog pointer, index discovery path and tracked-run-tree convention after the prospective source set was frozen. The current independent pure gate did not review that publication topology. It should not be used as a silent workaround for deterministic index regeneration.

Decision: **NO_GO_PUBLICATION_ROUTING_BEFORE_NATIVE** for the frozen I04.var03 v1.0.0 candidate. Preserve its contract, 119 files, manifest, root PURE receipts and prior GO_PURE_PREFLIGHT as exact historical evidence. No actual SSH preflight or SIMLOX child was dispatched. A new, distinctly versioned prospective package and run ID can include an explicit postrun exclusion policy for publication docs/index before any freeze, then receive fresh source, actual SSH5 zero-native preflight and independent GO_PRELAUNCH. The frozen v1.0.0 native approval cannot be inherited.
